        <mxCell id="r899" parent="61" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=9;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" value="&lt;b&gt;C1 100 µF&lt;/b&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="14" width="120" x="1170" y="682" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="r900" parent="61" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=20;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#666666;rounded=1;" value="&lt;b style=&#x27;font-size:20px&#x27;&gt;Breadboard wiring — MB102, hole by hole · AD8232 ECG + OLED&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&#x27;font-size:11px;color:#555555&#x27;&gt;Current version. Numbered circles match the wire list below. The MAX30102 and the I²C pull-up resistors are gone; the OLED keeps GPIO8/GPIO9 and is now the only device on that bus. Columns 1–50 shown; your board has 63.&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="46" width="1480" x="110" y="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="r901" parent="61" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;rounded=1;" value="&lt;b&gt;How a breadboard joins holes:&lt;/b&gt; in the middle section the &lt;b&gt;five holes of one column on the same side of the channel (A–E, or F–J) are one electrical node&lt;/b&gt;. The four long rails run the other way — the whole strip is one node. That is why a pin in row B and a wire in row A of the same column are connected." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="1480" x="110" y="790" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="r902" parent="61" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;verticalAlign=top;" value="&lt;table cellpadding=&#x27;4&#x27; cellspacing=&#x27;0&#x27; style=&#x27;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:10.5px;width:100%&#x27;&gt;&lt;tr style=&#x27;background:#dae8fc&#x27;&gt;&lt;th align=&#x27;left&#x27;&gt;#&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th align=&#x27;left&#x27;&gt;Colour&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th align=&#x27;left&#x27;&gt;From hole&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th align=&#x27;left&#x27;&gt;To hole&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th align=&#x27;left&#x27;&gt;Net&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th align=&#x27;left&#x27;&gt;Why&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&#x27;background:#fff4f4&#x27;&gt;&lt;td colspan=&#x27;6&#x27;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stage 1 — power. Wire these, plug in USB, measure, unplug.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;orange&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A1&lt;/b&gt; (J1 pin 1 = 3V3)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;bottom + rail, col 1&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;+3.3 V&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Makes the + rail 3.3 V. Nothing else may feed it&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&#x27;background:#f8f8f8&#x27;&gt;&lt;td&gt;2&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;black&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A22&lt;/b&gt; (J1 pin 22 = GND)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;bottom − rail, col 22&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;GND&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Common return for everything&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;3&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;red&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A21&lt;/b&gt; (J1 pin 21 = 5V)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A46&lt;/b&gt; (DRV8833 VCC)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;+5 V&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;Point to point — 5 V never touches a rail&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&#x27;background:#fff4f4&#x27;&gt;&lt;td colspan=&#x27;6&#x27;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stage 2 — the AD8232 ECG. 6 wires, no resistors.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;4&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;black&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A26&lt;/b&gt; (AD8232 GND)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;bottom − rail, col 26&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;GND&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Same ground as the ESP32&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&#x27;background:#f8f8f8&#x27;&gt;&lt;td&gt;5&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;orange&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A27&lt;/b&gt; (AD8232 3.3V)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;bottom + rail, col 27&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;+3.3 V&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;3.3 V only — never 5 V&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;6&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;green&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A5&lt;/b&gt; (J1 pin 5 = GPIO5)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A28&lt;/b&gt; (AD8232 OUTPUT)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;ECG&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;The analog heart signal. GPIO5 is an ADC1 pin, so it keeps working with Wi-Fi on&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&#x27;background:#f8f8f8&#x27;&gt;&lt;td&gt;7&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;blue&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A6&lt;/b&gt; (J1 pin 6 = GPIO6)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A30&lt;/b&gt; (AD8232 LO+)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;leads-off&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Goes HIGH when an electrode is off&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;8&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;cyan&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A7&lt;/b&gt; (J1 pin 7 = GPIO7)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A29&lt;/b&gt; (AD8232 LO−)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;leads-off&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Same for the other electrode&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&#x27;background:#f8f8f8&#x27;&gt;&lt;td&gt;9&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;orange&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A31&lt;/b&gt; (AD8232 SDN)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;bottom + rail, col 31&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;+3.3 V&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Holds the chip on — LOW would shut it down&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&#x27;background:#fff4f4&#x27;&gt;&lt;td colspan=&#x27;6&#x27;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stage 3 — the OLED screen. 4 wires. Then the screen lights up at boot.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;10&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;black&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A36&lt;/b&gt; (OLED GND)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;bottom − rail, col 36&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;GND&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;—&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&#x27;background:#f8f8f8&#x27;&gt;&lt;td&gt;11&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;orange&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A37&lt;/b&gt; (OLED VCC)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;bottom + rail, col 37&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;+3.3 V&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Display power (the module is 3.3–5 V tolerant)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;12&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;yellow&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A15&lt;/b&gt; (J1 pin 15 = GPIO9)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A38&lt;/b&gt; (OLED SCL)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;I²C clock&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Straight to the ESP32 — there is no second I²C device any more&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&#x27;background:#f8f8f8&#x27;&gt;&lt;td&gt;13&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;brown&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A12&lt;/b&gt; (J1 pin 12 = GPIO8)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A39&lt;/b&gt; (OLED SDA)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;I²C data&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;The screen answers at address 0x3C (a few boards use 0x3D)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&#x27;background:#fff4f4&#x27;&gt;&lt;td colspan=&#x27;6&#x27;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stage 4 — motor. Unchanged from the old layout.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;14&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;black&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A45&lt;/b&gt; (DRV8833 GND)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;bottom − rail, col 45&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;GND&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;Driver must share ground with the ESP32&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&#x27;background:#f8f8f8&#x27;&gt;&lt;td&gt;15&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;purple&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A4&lt;/b&gt; (J1 pin 4 = GPIO4)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A48&lt;/b&gt; (DRV8833 IN1)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;PWM&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Speed / alert pattern&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;16&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;black&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A47&lt;/b&gt; (DRV8833 IN2)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;bottom − rail, col 47&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;GND&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Ties direction low&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&#x27;background:#f8f8f8&#x27;&gt;&lt;td&gt;17&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;C1&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;B46&lt;/b&gt; (VCC node, + leg)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;bottom − rail, col 41&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;decouple&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;100 µF — striped leg to the − rail&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;18&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;orange &lt;i&gt;(dashed)&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;col 43, rows F–J&lt;/b&gt; (SLEEP)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;top + rail, col 43&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;+3.3 V&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;Only if SLEEP is not already high.&lt;/b&gt; Many boards tie it high on board — measure SLEEP to GND first. Motor silent? Try this&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&#x27;background:#f8f8f8&#x27;&gt;&lt;td&gt;18a&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;orange &lt;i&gt;(dashed)&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;bottom + rail&lt;/b&gt;, col 50&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;top + rail&lt;/b&gt;, col 50&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;+3.3 V&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Feeds the top + rail so 18 can reach SLEEP. Needed only together with 18&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;19&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;motor lead&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;col 44, rows F–J&lt;/b&gt; (OUT1)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;M1 lead 1&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;motor&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Polarity irrelevant&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&#x27;background:#f8f8f8&#x27;&gt;&lt;td&gt;20&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;motor lead&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;col 45, rows F–J&lt;/b&gt; (OUT2)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;M1 lead 2&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;motor&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;Never to a rail or a GPIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&#x27;background:#fff4f4&#x27;&gt;&lt;td colspan=&#x27;6&#x27;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Electrodes — not on the breadboard&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;E&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;3-lead cable&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;3.5 mm jack on the AD8232&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;RA / LA / RL gel pads&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;body&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;RA below the wearer&#x27;s right collarbone · LA below the left collarbone · RL on the lower right ribs. Go by the letters on the clips. &lt;b&gt;Pads on a person only on power-bank power, or with the laptop on battery, charger unplugged.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="610" width="1480" x="110" y="836" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="r903" parent="61" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;rounded=1;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;" value="&lt;b&gt;Check these against your actual parts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&#x27;font-size:10px&#x27;&gt;ESP32 pin positions are exact — taken from the Espressif DevKitC-1 pinout. J1 is the header carrying 3V3, GPIO4–GPIO7, 5V and GND, and its pin n sits in column n.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;The AD8232&#x27;s pin order varies between boards.&lt;/b&gt; The order drawn here (GND · 3.3V · OUTPUT · LO− · LO+ · SDN) is the common one. Read your module&#x27;s silkscreen and follow the labels; if the order differs, the columns change but the wires do not.&lt;br&gt;Some AD8232 boards have no SDN pin at all — then skip wire 9, the chip is always on.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;OLED:&lt;/b&gt; 4 pins, GND · VCC · SCL · SDA (some boards swap SCL/SDA — follow the print on the board). It answers at 0x3C; if the screen stays blank, try 0x3D (OLED_ADDR in src/main.cpp).&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="210" width="730" x="110" y="1466" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="r904" parent="61" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;rounded=1;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;" value="&lt;b&gt;Rules this layout follows&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&#x27;font-size:10px&#x27;&gt;&lt;b&gt;One voltage per rail.&lt;/b&gt; The + rail is 3.3 V and only 3.3 V; 5 V travels on its own wire so it can never reach the AD8232.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Single ground reference.&lt;/b&gt; Every GND lands on the same − rail — the ECG is measured against it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;No pull-up resistors.&lt;/b&gt; The AD8232&#x27;s outputs are driven, the firmware turns on the ESP32&#x27;s own pull-ups on GPIO6/7, and the OLED module brings its own I²C pull-ups.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Motor away from the sensor.&lt;/b&gt; Keep M1 and its leads off the board and at least 10 cm from the AD8232 and the electrode cable — motor noise shows up in the ECG.&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="210" width="730" x="860" y="1466" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="mlnote" parent="61" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;" value="&lt;b&gt;Does the ML model change this circuit?&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; No. The ECG beat-shape model (PTB heartbeats) is compiled into the firmware as plain C: 110&amp;nbsp;KB of flash (1.4&amp;nbsp;% of the 8&amp;nbsp;MB on the N8R8), an MLP 187→128→32→1, no ML library, no extra chip and no extra wire. At boot it scores 8 test beats stored in flash and both dashboards show the result. It does &lt;b&gt;not&lt;/b&gt; read the live AD8232 signal (it does not transfer beyond the PTB recordings yet) — the DANGER alert comes from the 60–100&amp;nbsp;BPM threshold on the measured heart rate." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="150" width="1480" x="110" y="1700" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="wifinote" parent="61" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d0e0e3;strokeColor=#0b5394;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;" value="&lt;b&gt;Do the Wi-Fi/Bluetooth dashboards, pairing and power bank change this wiring?&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; No. Wi-Fi and Bluetooth LE are the radio built into the ESP32-S3 module, so the laptop website, the phone app, the Bluetooth app, pairing and the fake-BPM demo input are all firmware — no extra part and no extra wire. They add about 110&amp;nbsp;mA on average plus brief ~350&amp;nbsp;mA transmit bursts — ~190&amp;nbsp;mA idle (the OLED adds ~20&amp;nbsp;mA), which is why the suit runs from a power bank rather than a laptop port. The OLED, the website and the phone app all show the same status, and so does the Serial Monitor." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="170" width="1480" x="110" y="1870" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rD48" parent="61" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=8;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" value="IN1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="14" width="52" x="1386" y="503" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rU45" parent="61" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=8;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" value="OUT2" vertex="1">
