  <diagram id="pg-circuit" name="1 - Demo-1 Circuit (old: MAX30102)">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1600" dy="1000" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1700" pageHeight="2700" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="title" value="&lt;b style='font-size:22px'&gt;SereniSuit — Demo 1 Circuit&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style='font-size:14px'&gt;Fingertip pulse → BPM on the website + phone app → DANGER banner + vibration alert&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style='font-size:11px;color:#555555'&gt;ESP32-S3-DevKitC-1-N8R8 · MAX30102 · DRV8833 · vibration motor — all values are design targets, verify against your exact modules&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style='font-size:11px;color:#0b5394'&gt;&lt;b&gt;+ Wi-Fi &amp;amp; Bluetooth dashboards (added):&lt;/b&gt; laptop + phone pair at the same time (Wi-Fi or Bluetooth LE) and show the live reading · remote sensor ON/OFF · fake-BPM demo input · runs from a power bank, no laptop cable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style='font-size:11px;color:#b85450'&gt;&lt;b&gt;OLED removed from Demo 1&lt;/b&gt; to keep the wiring simple — it and its wires are greyed out. The status shows on the website + phone app (the board's RGB LED is not used).&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#666666;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="110" y="30" width="1440" height="112" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="usb" value="&lt;b&gt;USB-C 5 V — power bank on demo day&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style='font-size:11px'&gt;Power bank ≥ 1 A output powers the whole suit — no laptop cable&lt;br&gt;Laptop USB is only for flashing, then unplug it&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;LiPo + TP4056 are NOT used in Demo 1&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="650" y="150" width="330" height="96" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="pullup" value="&lt;b&gt;I²C pull-ups ≈ 5 kΩ&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;(fit only if needed)&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style='font-size:10px'&gt;Per line: two 10 kΩ side by side — same column, same 3.3 V rail (the kit has no 4.7 kΩ; 10 k ∥ 10 k = 5 kΩ works the same). &lt;b&gt;Page 5 shows how.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;SDA → 3V3 and SCL → 3V3.&lt;br&gt;Many black MAX30102 boards pull I²C up to only &lt;b&gt;1.8 V&lt;/b&gt;, below the ESP32's 2.48 V logic-high threshold → &quot;sensor not found&quot;. These resistors fix that.&lt;br&gt;Source: KITS4CREATORS kit&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="110" y="150" width="300" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="max" value="&lt;b&gt;MAX30102&lt;/b&gt; &lt;span style='font-size:10px'&gt;(Techtonics, Amazon)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i style='font-size:11px'&gt;Fingertip pulse sensor — PPG&lt;/i&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;span style='font-size:11px'&gt;VIN&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;3.3 V&lt;/b&gt; (module has onboard LDO)&lt;br&gt;I²C address&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;0x57&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Supply&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;~6 mA (LED current 6.4 mA default)&lt;br&gt;Red + IR LED — Class 1, eye safe&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Pins used:&lt;/b&gt; VIN · GND · SDA · SCL&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Leave open:&lt;/b&gt; INT · IRD · RD&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="110" y="330" width="300" height="200" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="oled" value="&lt;b&gt;SSD1306 OLED 0.96&amp;quot;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;span style='font-size:10px'&gt;(Robocraze)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i style='font-size:11px'&gt;128 × 64 display — BPM + status&lt;/i&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;span style='font-size:11px'&gt;VCC&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;3.3 V&lt;/b&gt; (module is 3.3–5 V tolerant)&lt;br&gt;I²C address&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;0x3C&lt;/b&gt; (try 0x3D if blank)&lt;br&gt;Supply&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;~20 mA typ, 25 mA peak&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Pins used:&lt;/b&gt; VCC · GND · SDA · SCL&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;4-pin module = I²C, wire as shown.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;7-pin module = SPI → see page 2 note&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;opacity=22;textOpacity=30;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="110" y="580" width="300" height="200" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="esp" value="&lt;b&gt;ESP32-S3-DevKitC-1-N8R8&lt;/b&gt; &lt;span style='font-size:10px'&gt;(Robu)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i style='font-size:11px'&gt;Main controller — sensing, decision, drive&lt;/i&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;span style='font-size:11px'&gt;Logic level&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;3.3 V&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;3V3 rail (onboard LDO)&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;≤ 500 mA&lt;br&gt;5V pin (straight from USB-C)&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;= power bank / laptop port&lt;br&gt;GPIO drive&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;20 mA rec. · &lt;b&gt;40 mA absolute max&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;b style='font-size:11px'&gt;PINS USED IN DEMO 1&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style='font-size:11px'&gt;&lt;b&gt;GPIO8&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;→ SDA&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;i&gt;(I²C, shared)&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;GPIO9&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;→ SCL&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;i&gt;(I²C, shared)&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;GPIO4&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;→ DRV8833 IN1&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;i&gt;(PWM out)&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;3V3&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;→ MAX30102 VIN&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;5V&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;→ DRV8833 VCC&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;GND&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;→ common ground, all modules&lt;/span&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;span style='font-size:10px'&gt;Confirm GPIO8/9 are your board's I²C defaults, or pass them explicitly: &lt;i&gt;Wire.begin(8, 9)&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="650" y="330" width="330" height="450" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="cap" value="&lt;b&gt;100 µF / 16 V electrolytic&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style='font-size:10px'&gt;Wired across DRV8833 &lt;b&gt;VCC ↔ GND&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;br&gt;Absorbs the motor's ~250 mA inrush so the ESP32 does not brown out and the I²C bus does not glitch when the alert fires.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b style='color:#b85450'&gt;⚠ POLARITY: striped leg (−) to GND.&lt;/b&gt; Reversed electrolytics vent.&lt;br&gt;Source: KITS4CREATORS kit&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1240" y="150" width="310" height="140" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="drv" value="&lt;b&gt;DRV8833 dual H-bridge&lt;/b&gt; &lt;span style='font-size:10px'&gt;(Robu)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i style='font-size:11px'&gt;Motor driver — never skip this stage&lt;/i&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;span style='font-size:11px'&gt;VCC supply&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;2.7 – 10.8 V&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;→ &lt;b&gt;use 5 V&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Logic inputs&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;1.8 – 5 V → &lt;b&gt;3.3 V is safe&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Output&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;1.5 A RMS / 2 A peak per channel&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Internal body diodes = flyback protection&lt;br&gt;already built in — no external diode needed&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;span style='font-size:11px'&gt;VCC&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;← ESP32 5V&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;GND ← common GND&lt;br&gt;IN1 ← GPIO4 (PWM)&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;IN2 ← GND&lt;br&gt;OUT1 / OUT2 → motor&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Channel B unused&lt;br&gt;SLEEP (EEP) → 3V3 &lt;i&gt;if no onboard pull-up&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1240" y="330" width="310" height="250" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="motor" value="&lt;b&gt;Encapsulated vibration motor&lt;/b&gt; &lt;span style='font-size:10px'&gt;(Robu)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i style='font-size:11px'&gt;8000 ± 2000 RPM — the haptic alert&lt;/i&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;span style='font-size:11px'&gt;Rated&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;3 V DC&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;·&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Run&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;~80–100 mA&lt;br&gt;Inrush / stall&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;up to ~250 mA&lt;br&gt;Fed from the 5 V VCC rail at &lt;b&gt;PWM duty ≤ 60 %&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;→ V&lt;sub&gt;avg&lt;/sub&gt; ≈ &lt;b&gt;3.0 V&lt;/b&gt;, inside rating&lt;br&gt;Polarity: either way — direction is irrelevant&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Alt: Electrobot 3 V coin motor (Amazon)&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1240" y="630" width="310" height="160" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-usb" value="&lt;b&gt;5 V DC&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;500 mA" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=3;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="usb" target="esp">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-max" value="&lt;b&gt;I²C bus @ 0x57&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;SDA → GPIO8&lt;br&gt;SCL → GPIO9&lt;br&gt;VIN ← 3V3 · GND" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=3;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="max" target="esp">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-oled" value="&lt;b&gt;Same 2 I²C wires @ 0x3C&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;SDA → GPIO8&lt;br&gt;SCL → GPIO9&lt;br&gt;VCC ← 3V3 · GND" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=3;fontSize=11;opacity=22;textOpacity=30;" edge="1" parent="1" source="oled" target="esp">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-drv" value="&lt;b&gt;GPIO4 → IN1&lt;/b&gt; (PWM 5 kHz, duty ≤ 60 %)&lt;br&gt;GND → IN2 · 5V → VCC · GND → GND" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#9673a6;strokeWidth=3;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="esp" target="drv">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-motor" value="&lt;b&gt;OUT1 / OUT2&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;≈ 3.0 V avg · 80–100 mA" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=3;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="drv" target="motor">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-cap" value="100 µF across VCC–GND" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#d6b656;strokeWidth=2;dashed=1;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="cap" target="drv">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-pullup" value="only if sensor not detected" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#d6b656;strokeWidth=2;dashed=1;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="pullup" target="max">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="hdr-crit" value="&lt;b&gt;CRITICAL VALUES AT A GLANCE&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=13;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="110" y="820" width="400" height="26" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="crit" value="&lt;table cellpadding='5' cellspacing='0' style='border-collapse:collapse;font-size:11px;width:100%'&gt;&lt;tr style='background:#dae8fc'&gt;&lt;th align='left'&gt;Quantity&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th align='left'&gt;Value&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th align='left'&gt;Why it matters&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Logic level&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;3.3 V&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Every signal pin on this board is 3.3 V — never feed a 5 V signal into a GPIO.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style='background:#f8f8f8'&gt;&lt;td&gt;Sensor supply&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;3.3 V&lt;/b&gt; from 3V3 pin&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;The MAX30102 runs at 3.3 V, the same level as the ESP32 I²C pins.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Motor supply (VCC)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;5 V&lt;/b&gt; from 5V pin&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;DRV8833 needs ≥ 2.7 V; 5 V gives headroom for PWM control.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style='background:#f8f8f8'&gt;&lt;td&gt;Motor drive voltage&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;≈ 3.0 V avg&lt;/b&gt; (duty ≤ 60 %)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Motor is rated 3 V. 100 % duty at 5 V overdrives it and shortens its life.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Motor current&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;80–100 mA run, &lt;b&gt;~250 mA inrush&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Far above the 40 mA GPIO limit — this is why the DRV8833 exists.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style='background:#f8f8f8'&gt;&lt;td&gt;GPIO limit&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;20 mA rec · &lt;b&gt;40 mA abs max&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Exceeding it kills the pin permanently.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;I²C addresses&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;0x57&lt;/b&gt; sensor&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;The only chip on the two I²C wires (the 0x3C OLED is not fitted).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style='background:#f8f8f8'&gt;&lt;td&gt;Bulk capacitor&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;100 µF / 16 V&lt;/b&gt; across VCC–GND&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Stops the motor kick from browning out the ESP32 mid-demo.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Total current draw&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;~170 mA idle, ~650 mA brief peak &lt;i&gt;(Wi-Fi + Bluetooth on)&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Power bank rated ≥ 1 A (most give 2 A). Wi-Fi transmit power is set to 11 dBm to trim the peaks.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style='background:#f8f8f8'&gt;&lt;td&gt;Alert threshold&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;60 – 100 BPM = normal&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Standard resting adult range; outside it → DANGER + vibration.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fillColor=#ffffff;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="110" y="850" width="1440" height="300" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="t1" value="&lt;b style='font-size:20px'&gt;SCHEMATIC — component symbols and wiring&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=20;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#666666;rounded=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="110" y="1240" width="1440" height="40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="t2" value="&lt;b&gt;Read it like any schematic:&lt;/b&gt; a &lt;b&gt;filled dot&lt;/b&gt; means the wires are joined. Wires that simply cross with &lt;b&gt;no dot are NOT connected&lt;/b&gt;. Wire colours: &lt;span style='color:#CC0000'&gt;&lt;b&gt;+5 V&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt; · &lt;span style='color:#E07B00'&gt;&lt;b&gt;+3.3 V&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt; · &lt;b&gt;GND&lt;/b&gt; · &lt;span style='color:#1F6FD0'&gt;&lt;b&gt;SDA&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt; · &lt;span style='color:#2E8B2E'&gt;&lt;b&gt;SCL&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt; · &lt;span style='color:#8B2FBE'&gt;&lt;b&gt;PWM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt; · &lt;span style='color:#B85450'&gt;&lt;b&gt;motor&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="110" y="1286" width="1440" height="26" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
