        <mxCell id="d896" parent="61" style="ellipse;html=1;fillColor=#101010;strokeColor=none;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="11" width="11" x="1354" y="563.5" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="d897" parent="61" style="ellipse;html=1;fillColor=#101010;strokeColor=none;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="11" width="11" x="1224.5" y="720.5" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n898" parent="61" style="ellipse;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#101010;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;fontColor=#101010;" value="&lt;b&gt;18&lt;/b&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="22" width="22" x="1173" y="645" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="r899" parent="61" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=9;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" value="&lt;b&gt;C1 100 µF&lt;/b&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="14" width="120" x="1170" y="682" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="r900" parent="61" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=20;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#666666;rounded=1;" value="&lt;b style='font-size:20px'&gt;Breadboard wiring — MB102, hole by hole&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style='font-size:11px'&gt;Numbered circles match the wire list below. &lt;b style='color:#b85450'&gt;OLED (U3) and wires 8–11 removed from Demo 1 — greyed out, do not fit them.&lt;/b&gt; Columns 1–50 shown; your board has 63.&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="46" width="1480" x="110" y="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="r901" parent="61" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;rounded=1;" value="&lt;b&gt;How a breadboard joins holes:&lt;/b&gt; in the middle section the &lt;b&gt;five holes of one column on the same side of the channel (A–E, or F–J) are one electrical node&lt;/b&gt;. The four long rails run the other way — the whole strip is one node. That is why a pin in row B and a wire in row A of the same column are connected." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="1480" x="110" y="790" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="r902" parent="61" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;verticalAlign=top;" value="&lt;table cellpadding='4' cellspacing='0' style='border-collapse:collapse;font-size:10.5px;width:100%'&gt;&lt;tr style='background:#dae8fc'&gt;&lt;th align='left'&gt;#&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th align='left'&gt;Colour&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th align='left'&gt;From hole&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th align='left'&gt;To hole&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th align='left'&gt;Net&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th align='left'&gt;Why&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style='background:#fff4f4'&gt;&lt;td colspan='6'&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stage 1 — power. Wire these, plug in USB, measure, unplug.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;orange&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A1&lt;/b&gt; (J1 pin 1 = 3V3)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;bottom + rail, col 1&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;+3.3 V&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Makes the + rail 3.3 V. Nothing else may feed it&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style='background:#f8f8f8'&gt;&lt;td&gt;2&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;black&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A22&lt;/b&gt; (J1 pin 22 = GND)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;bottom − rail, col 22&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;GND&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Common return for everything&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;3&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;red&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A21&lt;/b&gt; (J1 pin 21 = 5V)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A46&lt;/b&gt; (DRV8833 VCC)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;+5 V&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;Point to point — 5 V never touches a rail&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style='background:#fff4f4'&gt;&lt;td colspan='6'&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stage 2 — I²C. Then run an I²C scanner; it must find 0x57.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;4&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;orange&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A26&lt;/b&gt; (MAX30102 VIN)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;bottom + rail, col 26&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;+3.3 V&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Sensor power&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style='background:#f8f8f8'&gt;&lt;td&gt;5&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;black&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A27&lt;/b&gt; (MAX30102 GND)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;bottom − rail, col 27&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;GND&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;—&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;6&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;green&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A15&lt;/b&gt; (J1 pin 15 = GPIO9)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A28&lt;/b&gt; (MAX30102 SCL)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;SCL&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;I²C clock&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style='background:#f8f8f8'&gt;&lt;td&gt;7&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;blue&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A12&lt;/b&gt; (J1 pin 12 = GPIO8)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A29&lt;/b&gt; (MAX30102 SDA)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;SDA&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;I²C data&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style='color:#aaaaaa'&gt;&lt;td&gt;8&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;black&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A36&lt;/b&gt; (OLED GND)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;bottom − rail, col 36&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;GND&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;— &lt;i&gt;— removed&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style='color:#aaaaaa'&gt;&lt;td&gt;9&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;orange&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A37&lt;/b&gt; (OLED VCC)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;bottom + rail, col 37&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;+3.3 V&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Display power &lt;i&gt;— removed&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style='color:#aaaaaa'&gt;&lt;td&gt;10&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;green&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A38&lt;/b&gt; (OLED SCL)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;C28&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;SCL&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;Daisy-chain.&lt;/b&gt; C28 is the same node as A28 &lt;i&gt;— removed&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style='color:#aaaaaa'&gt;&lt;td&gt;11&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;blue&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A39&lt;/b&gt; (OLED SDA)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;C29&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;SDA&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Daisy-chain, same node as A29 &lt;i&gt;— removed&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style='background:#fff4f4'&gt;&lt;td colspan='6'&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stage 3 — motor. Only after the scanner passes.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;12&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;black&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A45&lt;/b&gt; (DRV8833 GND)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;bottom − rail, col 45&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;GND&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;Driver must share ground with the ESP32&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style='background:#f8f8f8'&gt;&lt;td&gt;13&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;purple&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A4&lt;/b&gt; (J1 pin 4 = GPIO4)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A48&lt;/b&gt; (DRV8833 IN1)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;PWM&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Speed / alert pattern&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;14&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;black&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;A47&lt;/b&gt; (DRV8833 IN2)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;bottom − rail, col 47&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;GND&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Ties direction low&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style='background:#f8f8f8'&gt;&lt;td&gt;15&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;orange &lt;i&gt;(dashed)&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;col 43, rows F–J&lt;/b&gt; (SLEEP)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;top + rail, col 43  (+ link the two + rails)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;+3.3 V&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;Only if SLEEP is not already high.&lt;/b&gt; Many boards tie it high with the on-board J1 jumper &amp;mdash; measure SLEEP to GND first. Motor silent? Try this&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style='background:#f8f8f8'&gt;&lt;td&gt;15a&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;orange &lt;i&gt;(dashed)&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;bottom + rail&lt;/b&gt;, col 50&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;top + rail&lt;/b&gt;, col 50&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;+3.3 V&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Feeds the top + rail so 15 can reach SLEEP. Needed only together with 15&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;16&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;motor lead&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;col 44, rows F–J&lt;/b&gt; (OUT1)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;M1 lead 1&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;motor&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Polarity irrelevant&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style='background:#f8f8f8'&gt;&lt;td&gt;17&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;motor lead&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;col 45, rows F–J&lt;/b&gt; (OUT2)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;M1 lead 2&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;motor&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;Never to a rail or a GPIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;18&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;C1&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;B46&lt;/b&gt; (VCC node, + leg)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;bottom − rail, col 41&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;decouple&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;100 µF — striped leg to the − rail&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style='background:#fff4f4'&gt;&lt;td colspan='6'&gt;&lt;b&gt;Only if the I²C scan cannot find 0x57&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;19&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;R1 10 kΩ ∥ 10 kΩ&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;B29&lt;/b&gt; (SDA node)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;bottom + rail&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;pull-up&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Two 10 kΩ side by side: same column, same + rail (= 5 kΩ, see page 5). Lifts SDA to a real 3.3 V high&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style='background:#f8f8f8'&gt;&lt;td&gt;20&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;R2 10 kΩ ∥ 10 kΩ&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;B28&lt;/b&gt; (SCL node)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;bottom + rail&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;pull-up&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Same for SCL&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="610" width="1480" x="110" y="836" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="r903" parent="61" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;rounded=1;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;" value="&lt;b style='font-size:13px'&gt;Check these against your actual parts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;span style='font-size:11px'&gt;&lt;b&gt;ESP32 pin positions are exact&lt;/b&gt; — taken from the Espressif DevKitC-1 pinout. J1 is the header carrying 3V3, GPIO4, GPIO8, GPIO9, 5V and GND, and its pin &lt;i&gt;n&lt;/i&gt; sits in column &lt;i&gt;n&lt;/i&gt; when you seat pin 1 at column 1. Confirm which physical end is pin 1 by finding the two 3V3 pins — they are pins 1 and 2.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;b&gt;DRV8833 (12-pin board).&lt;/b&gt; Pin names here match the silkscreen: &lt;b&gt;IN1 IN2 VCC GND IN3 IN4&lt;/b&gt; on one long edge, &lt;b&gt;SLEEP OUT1 OUT2 OUT3 OUT4 FAULT&lt;/b&gt; on the other. VCC is the MOTOR supply (2.7–10.8 V) — give it 5 V. IN3/IN4/OUT3/OUT4 are channel B, unused. Seat it &lt;b&gt;silkscreen up&lt;/b&gt; with the IN edge in row E &amp;mdash; left to right you must read &lt;b&gt;IN4 IN3 GND VCC IN2 IN1&lt;/b&gt; in cols 43&amp;ndash;48, and &lt;b&gt;SLEEP OUT1 OUT2 OUT3 OUT4 FAULT&lt;/b&gt; across the channel. If you read IN1 first, the board is turned the wrong way; how far the OUT side reaches (row F, G, H, I or J) depends on your board's width — it does not matter, every hole F–J of a column is one node.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Module pin ORDER is assumed&lt;/b&gt; — MAX30102 as VIN·GND·SCL·SDA and the DRV8833 by label. These vary between sellers. Read your silkscreen; if the order differs, keep the wire's &lt;i&gt;destination pin name&lt;/i&gt; and move it to whichever column that name lands in.&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="210" width="730" x="110" y="1466" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="r904" parent="61" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;rounded=1;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;" value="&lt;b style='font-size:13px'&gt;Rules this layout follows&lt;/b&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;span style='font-size:11px'&gt;&lt;b&gt;One voltage per rail.&lt;/b&gt; The + rail is 3.3 V and only 3.3 V; 5 V travels on its own wire so it can never reach the sensor.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Single ground reference.&lt;/b&gt; Every GND lands on the same − rail, which reaches the ESP32 through wire 2.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Decoupling at the load.&lt;/b&gt; C1 sits on the DRV8833's own VCC node, not off at the supply end, so it can actually absorb the motor's inrush.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;No inductive load on a GPIO.&lt;/b&gt; The motor only ever touches OUT1/OUT2.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;One chip on the I²C wires.&lt;/b&gt; Only the MAX30102 sits on SDA/SCL now; the OLED was removed from Demo 1.&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="210" width="730" x="860" y="1466" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="mlnote" parent="61" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;" value="&lt;b style='font-size:13px'&gt;Does the ML model change this circuit? &amp;nbsp;No.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;span style='font-size:11px'&gt;The PPG arousal classifier is compiled into the firmware as plain C: &lt;b&gt;1.3&amp;nbsp;KB of flash&lt;/b&gt; (0.02&amp;nbsp;% of the 8&amp;nbsp;MB on the N8R8), 16 features, no ML library, well under 1&amp;nbsp;KB of RAM while it runs. It adds &lt;b&gt;no components, no wires and no measurable current&lt;/b&gt;. Every wire on this page is unchanged.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;In Demo&amp;nbsp;1 the model does not drive the motor.&lt;/b&gt; The live alert is a threshold on heart rate (60&amp;ndash;100&amp;nbsp;BPM) taken from the MAX30102 already on this board. At boot the model scores 8 saved 30-second PPG windows and shows the score on the dashboard (and over serial when a laptop is connected) &amp;mdash; proof that it executes on the MCU itself.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Phase&amp;nbsp;2 needs no new parts either.&lt;/b&gt; Scoring a live finger reuses this same MAX30102: extract HRV features on-device over 30&amp;nbsp;s and compare them against the wearer's own calm baseline. That is firmware work, not a board change.&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="150" width="1480" x="110" y="1700" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="wifinote" parent="61" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d0e0e3;strokeColor=#0b5394;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;" value="&lt;b style='font-size:13px'&gt;Do the Wi-Fi/Bluetooth dashboards, pairing and power bank change this wiring? &amp;nbsp;No.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;span style='font-size:11px'&gt;Wi-Fi and Bluetooth LE are the radio built into the ESP32-S3 module, so the laptop website, the phone app, the Bluetooth app, pairing and the fake-BPM demo input are all firmware &amp;mdash; &lt;b&gt;no new parts, no new wires, no extra GPIO&lt;/b&gt;. Every hole on this page stays as it is.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Power on demo day:&lt;/b&gt; plug a power bank (&amp;ge; 1&amp;nbsp;A output) into the DevKit's USB-C instead of the laptop. It feeds the same 5&amp;nbsp;V pin and 3V3 regulator, so the Stage&amp;nbsp;1 rail checks read the same. Wi-Fi + Bluetooth add about 110&amp;nbsp;mA on average plus brief ~350&amp;nbsp;mA transmit bursts &amp;mdash; ~190&amp;nbsp;mA idle and ~650&amp;nbsp;mA peak in total, easy for a power bank but tight for a 500&amp;nbsp;mA laptop port. Use the laptop only to flash, then unplug it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;No laptop cable needed at the review:&lt;/b&gt; the Wi-Fi name, password and address are fixed (SereniSuit-Demo · seresuit123 · http://192.168.4.1; Bluetooth: SereniSuit) ; once the laptop and the phone connect, both screens show &amp;quot;Paired · 2 devices&amp;quot;.&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="170" width="1480" x="110" y="1870" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rD48" parent="61" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=8;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" value="IN1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="14" width="52" x="1386" y="503" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rU45" parent="61" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=8;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" value="OUT2" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="14" width="52" x="1308" y="408" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rU46" parent="61" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=8;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" value="OUT3" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="14" width="52" x="1334" y="408" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rU47" parent="61" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=8;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" value="OUT4" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="14" width="52" x="1360" y="408" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rU48" parent="61" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=8;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" value="FAULT" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="14" width="52" x="1386" y="408" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="w15a" edge="1" parent="61" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;curved=0;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#E07B00;strokeWidth=3;dashed=1;">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint x="1464" y="700" as="sourcePoint" />
            <mxPoint x="1464" y="245" as="targetPoint" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n15a" parent="61" style="ellipse;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#E07B00;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;fontColor=#E07B00;" value="15a" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="22" width="26" x="1474" y="450" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      <mxCell id="d15a694" value="" style="ellipse;html=1;fillColor=#E07B00;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="61"><mxGeometry x="1458" y="694" width="11" height="11" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="d15a239" value="" style="ellipse;html=1;fillColor=#E07B00;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="61"><mxGeometry x="1458" y="239" width="11" height="11" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="dE48" value="" style="ellipse;html=1;fillColor=#9673a6;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="61"><mxGeometry x="1406" y="485" width="12" height="12" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="dF45" value="" style="ellipse;html=1;fillColor=#9673a6;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="61"><mxGeometry x="1328" y="433" width="12" height="12" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="dF46" value="" style="ellipse;html=1;fillColor=#9673a6;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="61"><mxGeometry x="1354" y="433" width="12" height="12" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="dF47" value="" style="ellipse;html=1;fillColor=#9673a6;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="61"><mxGeometry x="1380" y="433" width="12" height="12" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="dF48" value="" style="ellipse;html=1;fillColor=#9673a6;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="61"><mxGeometry x="1406" y="433" width="12" height="12" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="nf-oled4" value="OLED NOT FITTED&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:9px;font-weight:normal&quot;&gt;skip U3 + wires 8–11&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#b85450;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#b85450;fillColor=#ffffff;rounded=1;dashed=1;" vertex="1" parent="61"><mxGeometry x="1060" y="404" width="160" height="36" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="pg-breadboard-old-banner" value="&lt;b&gt;OLD PAGE — MAX30102 version.&lt;/b&gt; The sensor is now the AD8232 ECG: see page 0 for the current wiring." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;fontSize=13;" vertex="1" parent="61"><mxGeometry x="40" y="-90" width="760" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
      </root>
